    "# AQI-Cast India — Environment Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "**Notebook:** `00_environment_setup.ipynb`  \n",
    "**Phase:** 1 — Project Foundation  \n",
    "**Purpose:** Establish and validate a reproducible local development environment for AQI-Cast India.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Introduction\n",
    "\n",
    "AQI-Cast India is an end-to-end air-quality forecasting and ML engineering platform for Indian cities. This notebook is the foundation for the remaining development notebooks. It checks the active Python environment, verifies the planned technology stack, initializes the repository workspace, establishes shared project settings, configures reproducibility defaults, and records an environment report.\n",
    "\n",
    "The initial dataset is historical (approximately 2015–2020). The first project version is therefore designed for **historical replay and backtesting**. This notebook does not connect to a live pollution feed or claim to provide current AQI measurements.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "- Verify the Python interpreter and the notebook runtime.\n",
    "- Inspect the libraries used across data engineering, forecasting, applications, and MLOps.\n",
    "- Create the project directories required by the agreed architecture.\n",
    "- Establish shared constants, random seeds, and plotting defaults.\n",
    "- Check available CPU, memory, and optional GPU capabilities without requiring a GPU.\n",
    "- Create a starter configuration only when one does not already exist.\n",
    "- Save a concise environment report in the project's artifact area.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 3. Technical approach\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is intentionally **non-destructive**. It does not download the dataset, train models, install packages automatically, overwrite an existing configuration, or modify system-level settings. Missing dependencies are reported with an installation hint so that package installation remains an explicit user decision.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 4. Execution order\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the notebook from the repository root when possible. The project-root resolver also supports a kernel started from the `notebooks` directory. Execute cells from top to bottom in a fresh kernel for the most reliable environment report."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8a43324e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Project conventions\n",
    "\n",
    "| Convention | Project standard |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Primary target | `AQI` |\n",
    "| City identifier | `City` |\n",
    "| Observation date | `Date` |\n",
    "| Forecast horizons | 1–7 days |\n",
    "| Primary model | LightGBM Regressor |\n",
    "| Evaluation | Chronological validation and rolling-origin backtesting |\n",
    "| Visualization output | `images/` |\n",
    "| Generated artifact output | `artifacts/` |\n",
    "| Initial operating mode | Historical replay / backtesting |\n",
    "\n",
    "All notebook-generated charts must be exported to the image area, and generated data/model/report files must be stored in the artifact area. Notebook status messages must not print absolute or unnecessary relative filesystem paths."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c26a8502",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Import standard libraries and initialize runtime settings\n",
    "\n",
    "The first code cell uses only the Python standard library. Environment variables that influence child processes are set before importing numerical libraries where practical. `PYTHONHASHSEED` cannot retroactively change hashing in the already-running kernel; it is set here for child processes and future launches."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "18183673",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Runtime initialization completed.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import random\n",
    "import platform\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import shutil\n",
    "import importlib\n",
    "import importlib.util\n",
    "from importlib import metadata\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
    "from tempfile import NamedTemporaryFile\n",
    "\n",
    "# Shared project defaults. Keep these consistent across later notebooks.\n",
    "PROJECT_NAME = \"AQI-Cast India\"\n",
    "PROJECT_SLUG = \"aqi-cast-india\"\n",
    "RANDOM_SEED = 42\n",
    "FORECAST_HORIZONS = tuple(range(1, 8))\n",
    "TARGET_COLUMN = \"AQI\"\n",
    "CITY_COLUMN = \"City\"\n",
    "DATE_COLUMN = \"Date\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set process-level defaults without overriding user-managed settings.\n",
    "os.environ.setdefault(\"PYTHONHASHSEED\", str(RANDOM_SEED))\n",
    "os.environ.setdefault(\"OMP_NUM_THREADS\", str(max(1, min(8, os.cpu_count() or 1))))\n",
    "os.environ.setdefault(\"MKL_NUM_THREADS\", str(max(1, min(8, os.cpu_count() or 1))))\n",
    "os.environ.setdefault(\"OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS\", str(max(1, min(8, os.cpu_count() or 1))))\n",
    "\n",
    "random.seed(RANDOM_SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Runtime initialization completed.\")"
   ]
  },
